(
  'eeeeeeee-eeee-4eee-8eee-eeeeeeeeeeee',
  'local_page',
  'breakfast-near-civic-center-san-francisco',
  'Breakfast Near Civic Center San Francisco',
  'Plan breakfast near Civic Center with Turkish pastries, eggs, savory dishes, coffee and tea at Turquaz on Mission Street.',
  '[{"type":"html","html":"<p>Breakfast near Civic Center San Francisco can serve many kinds of mornings: a quick stop before work, a meeting before an appointment, or a longer table shared with friends. Turquaz is at 1198 Mission Street, giving guests a specific destination on the Mission corridor near the Civic Center area.</p><p>Transit schedules, traffic, parking rules and service hours can change. Check a current map and the restaurant hours on the day of your visit, especially around holidays or major events. Share the full street address with the group rather than relying only on a neighborhood label.</p><h2>Choose the pace before choosing the dishes</h2><p>A short breakfast works best when each person knows the time available. Coffee, tea and pastry may suit a quick visit. A relaxed morning can include eggs, cheese, olives, vegetables, bread and sweet elements, depending on the current menu. Tell the team about a firm departure time before ordering a larger spread.</p><p>Groups should decide whether they want individual plates or a shared table. A shared Turkish breakfast benefits from contrast: fresh vegetables and cheese, something warm, bread, preserves or honey, and tea. Ordering gradually can keep the table manageable and reduce waste.</p><h2>Plan around Civic Center appointments and events</h2><p>Allow a buffer between breakfast and a scheduled appointment, performance or meeting. Arrival times can vary when guests use different transit routes. One clear meeting time and the exact restaurant address make coordination easier.</p><p>If the group is arriving separately, ask everyone to communicate delays directly. The restaurant cannot predict transit disruptions or event traffic. Current transportation information should come from official or live mapping sources.</p><h3>Breakfast for a work meeting</h3><p>For a work conversation, clarify whether the priority is speed, privacy or a broader shared meal. A concise order can leave more time for discussion. A longer breakfast may work better when participants do not have an immediate appointment afterward.</p><h2>Confirm ingredients and current availability</h2><p>Pastries, breads and prepared dishes can contain wheat, dairy, eggs, nuts or other allergens. Guests with dietary restrictions should ask about the current recipe and kitchen practices. General descriptions of Turkish breakfast cannot confirm the ingredients in a particular dish.</p><p>Review the <a href=\"/menu\">live Turquaz menu</a> for current selections and prices. When the morning is tied to a specific schedule, <a href=\"/#reservation\">reserve a table</a> and include the correct party size. Contact the restaurant directly for larger groups or questions that the online form cannot cover.</p>"}]',
  'published',
  'Breakfast Near Civic Center San Francisco | Turquaz',
  'Plan breakfast near Civic Center San Francisco with Turkish pastries, eggs, savory plates, coffee and tea at Turquaz on Mission Street.',
  'https://www.turquazsf.com/assets/images/dish-pastries.jpeg',
  'Fresh Turkish pastries prepared for breakfast near Civic Center San Francisco',
  'breakfast near Civic Center San Francisco',
  'Turquaz',
  '2026-08-27T23:53:00.000Z',
  '2026-08-27T23:53:00.000Z',
  '2026-08-27T23:53:00.000Z'
