(
  'ffffffff-ffff-4fff-8fff-ffffffffffff',
  'local_page',
  'group-dining-near-civic-center',
  'Group Dining Near Civic Center San Francisco',
  'Organize group dining near Civic Center with practical guidance for timing, shared menus, dietary questions and reservations.',
  '[{"type":"html","html":"<p>Group dining near Civic Center works best when logistics are settled before anyone sits down. Turquaz is located at 1198 Mission Street in San Francisco. A clear address, realistic arrival time and accurate guest count help a lunch, dinner or team gathering begin smoothly.</p><p>This page provides planning guidance rather than a promise of availability or a fixed group package. Restaurant capacity, dishes, prices and service options can change. Confirm the current details directly for the date and party you are organizing.</p><h2>Start with the purpose and schedule</h2><p>A team lunch with a one-hour window needs a different plan from a birthday dinner or family gathering. Tell guests when to arrive and when the group must leave. If the meal comes before a Civic Center appointment, performance or event, leave enough time for ordering, eating and walking or traveling onward.</p><p>Share the exact Mission Street address. The broader neighborhood covers many blocks, and guests may approach from different transit stops or parking areas. Use current transportation information on the day of the meal because schedules and street conditions can change.</p><h2>Collect dietary questions early</h2><p>Ask attendees about allergies and dietary restrictions before making final menu decisions. Turkish cooking can include wheat, dairy, eggs, nuts, sesame, legumes, meat and other ingredients across bread, sauces, pastries and garnishes. The restaurant should confirm current recipes and kitchen practices; organizers should not infer safety from a dish name.</p><h3>Choose shared or individual service</h3><p>Meze, bread and several warm dishes can create a social shared table. Individual plates may be more practical when time is limited or preferences vary widely. A mixed approach can begin with a few shared dishes and allow guests to select their own main plate.</p><h2>Keep the order focused</h2><p>Variety does not require ordering every item. Choose contrasting dishes that cover vegetables, grains, bread and warm preparations according to the group. Ordering in stages can work for a relaxed dinner, while a coordinated order may better suit a scheduled lunch.</p><p>Select one organizer to communicate final counts and timing. That person should know who can answer questions on the day and how the group will handle separate or combined payment. Payment arrangements should be confirmed with the restaurant rather than assumed.</p><h2>Reserve the correct destination</h2><p>Check the <a href=\"/menu\">current Turquaz menu</a> for available dishes and prices. The online form can <a href=\"/#reservation\">reserve a table for up to 15 guests</a>. For larger parties, catering or event-specific arrangements, contact the restaurant directly and provide the date, desired time, guest count and service needs.</p><p>Before the gathering, reconfirm the number of guests and notify the restaurant of material changes. A concise plan gives the group more time to enjoy the table once everyone arrives.</p>"}]',
  'published',
  'Group Dining Near Civic Center San Francisco | Turquaz',
  'Organize group dining near Civic Center San Francisco with guidance for timing, shared dishes, dietary questions and reservations at Turquaz.',
  'https://www.turquazsf.com/assets/images/about-interior.jpeg',
  'Turquaz dining room arranged for group dining near Civic Center San Francisco',
  'group dining near Civic Center',
  'Turquaz',
  '2026-08-27T23:54:00.000Z',
  '2026-08-27T23:54:00.000Z',
  '2026-08-27T23:54:00.000Z'
